# Build output
build/
*.obj
*.exe
*.dll
*.ilk
*.pdb

# Headless frame-dump scratch
*.png
# ...but the README's pictures are kept.
!/images/*.png

# The ROM is user-supplied; never commit copyrighted content.
*.sfc
*.smc

# The player's top scores, kept in the working directory by the frontend (src/hiscore.h).
*.hiscore
*.hiscore.tmp
# The latest quick save, kept in the working directory by the frontend (src/quicksave.h).
*.quicksave
*.quicksave.tmp

# The player's settings and bindings, written by the frontend when there is
# none (src/config.h). It names their ROM's path; it is theirs.
/zamn.ini

# Music / audio output; never commit copyrighted content.
*.spc
*.wav

# Analysis output. Derived from the user's ROM and quoting it verbatim (the
# CDL, the .db runs in every listing), so it is regenerated, never committed.
# See docs/analysis-tools.md for the commands.
# Anchored: an unanchored "analysis/" would also swallow src/analysis/.
/analysis/
# ...and any second opinion generated beside it, e.g. from another movie.
/analysis[0-9]*/

# Byte-compiled Python from tools/
__pycache__/

# Editor / OS cruft
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
Thumbs.db
